# reduction-batch fixtures

Used by `tests/test_batch_from_coverage.py` and (later) integration tests.

- `new_coverage.csv` — three gap-fill rows (`test-a` … `test-c`).
- `sample.bc` — bitcode copied from `example/amd/new-test-1/` for parse_test_sh validation.

Row `test-b` has two `covered-points` (`0x3000;0x2000`) so tests can assert the lowest
address (`0x2000`) is chosen. Unit tests materialize `candidate_tests/<name>/test.sh`
with absolute llc and .bc paths under a temporary directory.
